# rhwp equation and line-end fixes for why-hwp, measured against Hangul 2024 output.
# Base: rhwp 7213ed1f9 after the source edits in wasm/patch-rhwp.sh and
# wasm/patches/rhwp-layout.patch, rhwp-layout2.patch, rhwp-layout3.patch and
# rhwp-layout4.patch; apply this after rhwp-layout4.patch.
# Zero-context diff (apply with git apply --unidiff-zero).
#
# - equation/font_frame_metrics.rs, script_fraction_frame.rs: HYhwpEQ line and
#   fraction frames for sizes outside the measured tables follow the rule the
#   tables' rows follow (height is the size rounded to a whole 96 dpi pixel,
#   the math axis is the frame's middle, the baseline 0.36 em below it), so a
#   fraction in a superscript is placed at body sizes such as 11 pt too.
# - equation/layout/limit_geometry.rs: a HYhwpEQ `lim` name shares the math
#   axis of the body line and its lower limit sits right under the name's line
#   frame.
# - equation/layout/cases_columns.rs: HYhwpEQ `cases` cells are aligned by the
#   middle of their frames, not by their baselines.
# - equation/svg_render.rs, variable_outline.rs, brace_stretch.rs,
#   accent_outline.rs, svg.rs, pdf.rs, document_core/queries/rendering.rs: in a
#   PDF export, the equation structures Hangul 2024 paints with HyhwpEQ glyphs
#   (rules of fractions, radicals and overlines up to 9 em, radical signs,
#   text-height parentheses, braces, a tall left brace without a right one
#   assembled from parts, roman function-name letters) are painted with those
#   glyphs when the PDF font database holds HyhwpEQ. Without the font the paths
#   are drawn as before.
# - layout/paragraph_layout.rs: a right-aligned line leaves its trailing
#   ideographic spaces (U+3000) out of the aligned width, as it does trailing
#   ASCII spaces.
# - layout/text_measurement.rs: U+2013, U+2265, U+300C and U+300D of an HFT
#   font advance a full em.
# - equation/layout.rs, font_frame_metrics.rs, script_fraction_frame.rs,
#   svg_render.rs, pdf.rs, layout/paragraph_layout.rs and
#   layout/text_measurement.rs cover these changes.
